- P9-A5 target looked at. A tinted montage shows a full head of hair in each of the four pictures. The color files have mean RGB about (50, 42, 37) in those regions, so the hair is black, as Pat's hair is.
- Hashes. All six SHA-256 values of P9-A4 and P9-A5 match. The manifest selects line v1 for the four Pat rows and line v2 for l2-w06-check-row-ten.
- CSS. student-book.ts:138 `.picture-box` is `0.6mm dashed`; .map-place 93, .perforation 221, .fold-line 228; readers.ts:619 `.tear-tick` is `left: -0.2mm` with `border-left: 0.4mm solid`; readers.ts:542 .fold-line; card-kit.ts:826 `.card-picture-empty` `0.4mm dashed`. Exactly three dashed rules remain in the student book after the change, so the P9-A6 test can pass.
- Resolver. picture-check.ts:614 holds resolveStorytimePictureFiles(folder, rows, kind); calls at readers.ts:196 and 216, student-book.ts:767, card-kit.ts:589 and 597; the type holds rowId, fileName, file; art-edge-fill.ts is the cited pattern; line 589 of student-book.ts holds the earliest-week rule.
